    "summary": "A cotton skirt cloth, a kain panjang, hand-drawn but quite crude, in very simple version of &#039;megamendung&#039; motif in blue and red against a reddish brown ground.  The motif is associated with Cirebon, but this example may well have been made elsewhere.  The cloth appears to have been waxed on one face only.  Warp ends hemmed by hand.   [Text written by Dr Fiona Kerlogue, Horniman Museum.]",
